flowchart TB
    classDef input fill:#fff0e6,stroke:#f97316,stroke-width:2px,color:#431407;
    classDef core fill:#eaf3ff,stroke:#1673c9,stroke-width:3px,color:#102a43;
    classDef output fill:#effbf3,stroke:#169c52,stroke-width:2px,color:#123c24;
    classDef feedback fill:#fff8db,stroke:#ca8a04,stroke-width:2px,color:#513600;

    subgraph A[1 · Range intent and commercial guardrails]
      direction LR
      Brief[Seasonal brief<br/>customer, trend, channel & price architecture] --> Lasts[Last strategy<br/>new lasts, carry-over & category role]
    end

    subgraph B[2 · SKU Dash — the master range builder]
      direction LR
      Range[Range architecture<br/>style, category, last, newness & carry-over] --> SKU[SKU creation<br/>colour, material, Upper 2 & imagery] --> Price[Style pricing<br/>landed cost, target margin & RRP suggestion] --> Spec[Development spec<br/>components, measurements & factory pack] --> Fit[Fitting & approval<br/>samples, fit notes & size recommendation]
    end

    subgraph C[3 · Controlled decisions and hand-offs]
      direction LR
      Buy[Buy plan<br/>channel/location quantities & buy sessions] --> PO[Production / purchase order<br/>confirmed cost, MOQ, supplier & ETA] --> Launch[E-commerce & retail launch<br/>product data, images, final RRP & assortment]
      Master[Product master / AP21<br/>style, SKU, colour codes & size range] --> Launch
    end

    subgraph D[4 · Post-launch learning loop]
      direction LR
      Trade[Trading signals<br/>sell-through, markdowns & customer feedback] --> Learn[Range review<br/>repeat, recolour, cancel or refine]
    end

    Lasts --> Range
    Price --> Buy
    SKU --> Master
    Spec --> PO
    Fit --> PO
    Launch --> Trade
    Learn -. informs next seasonal brief .-> Brief
    Trade -. price / cost / demand feedback .-> Price
    Trade -. fit and product feedback .-> Fit

    class Brief,Lasts input
    class Range,SKU,Price,Spec,Fit core
    class Buy,Master,PO,Launch output
    class Trade,Learn feedback
